# Design skills (project)

When designing or changing UI on in-scope pages (Home, About Us, Services, Events), **read and follow** the relevant skills under `.cursor/skills/` before writing UI code.

## Default stack (use together)

1. **frontend-design** — distinctive aesthetic direction; avoid templated AI looks
2. **design-taste-frontend** — layout, typography, motion, density dials (anti-slop)
3. **ui-ux-pro-max** — design-system search / style / palette / typography guidance
4. **emil-design-eng** — animation and micro-interaction quality
5. **impeccable** — design commands (`critique`, `polish`, `audit`, `animate`, etc.) and detector rules

Also respect existing project docs: `docs/OVA_WEBSITE_DESIGN_GUIDE.md` and OVA’s four objectives.

## When to pull specialized skills

| Need | Skill |
|------|--------|
| Redesign existing UI | `redesign-existing-projects` |
| Softer / premium polish | `high-end-visual-design` |
| Animation from scratch | `animate` |
| Review motion | `review-animations` |
| Find motion opportunities | `find-animation-opportunities` |
| Tailwind / shadcn styling | `ui-styling` |
| Brand voice / identity | `brand` |

## Hard constraints

- Prefer project visual language over generic SaaS/AI defaults (Inter-only, purple gradients, nested cards, emoji-as-icons).
- Keep scope to Home / About / Services / Events unless the user asks otherwise.
- After substantial UI changes, run an Impeccable-style pass: hierarchy, a11y, responsive, motion restraint.
